# On the live session, live-config grants its own `user` account
# passwordless sudo (/etc/sudoers.d/live) -- but that file is a
# live-only runtime artifact live-config writes at boot, never part of
# the actual installed filesystem Calamares copies. Any account
# Calamares creates (sudoersGroup: sudo, per calamares-settings-debian's
# users.conf) otherwise falls back to Debian's normal default: prompt
# for the invoking user's own password. That breaks kiosk operation --
# vpinos-menu needs to launch Hyprland/vpinball/vpinfe/calamares with zero
# interactive prompts. Scoped to vpinos-launch specifically (not blanket
# NOPASSWD: ALL) so a real password is still required for anything else
# run via sudo on an installed system.
%sudo ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/vpinos-launch

# vpinos-menu's own Shutdown option (systemctl poweroff, not the
# whole systemctl binary) -- a kiosk cabinet's only "log out" is
# physically powering it off; no polkit/logind config is assumed
# present or configured to already allow this for the local session,
# so this is scoped explicitly, same reasoning and same narrow-scope
# style as vpinos-launch above.
%sudo ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemctl poweroff

# vpinos-menu's Reboot option (systemctl reboot, not the whole
# systemctl binary) -- same reasoning and same narrow scope as the
# poweroff rule above.
%sudo ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemctl reboot

# vpinos-menu's Network Settings option (nmtui, editing/activating
# NetworkManager connections) -- confirmed directly against
# NetworkManager's own shipped polkit policy
# (org.freedesktop.NetworkManager.settings.modify.system): its
# <allow_active> default is auth_admin_keep, not yes, so even the
# locally logged-in console user isn't auto-authorized, and there's no
# polkit agent running in this raw console session to handle that
# prompt. Running nmtui as root via sudo sidesteps this entirely --
# polkit trivially authorizes a root-owned caller -- same reasoning and
# same narrow-scope style as the two rules above.
%sudo ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/nmtui

# vpinos-launch calls vpinos-gpu-driver.sh (every invocation, before
# starting Hyprland) to switch which GPU kernel module is bound, per
# the "GPU Driver" menu option. modprobe/rmmod need CAP_SYS_MODULE
# (root) -- scoped to this one dedicated script, not a blanket modprobe
# rule, so vpinos can't load/unload arbitrary kernel modules. Same
# narrow-scope reasoning as the three rules above.
%sudo ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: /usr/libexec/vpinos/vpinos-gpu-driver.sh

# vpinos-menu's Testing submenu's "SSH Password Authentication" option
# (live CD only) -- writing an sshd_config.d drop-in and restarting
# ssh.service both need root. Scoped to this one dedicated script, same
# narrow-scope reasoning as every other rule above.
%sudo ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: /usr/libexec/vpinos/vpinos-ssh-password-auth.sh

# vpinos-menu's VR > Setup > "Install VR components" option -- apt
# installs (WiVRn, adb, encoder libraries) and the system-wide OpenXR
# runtime pointer both need root. Scoped to this one dedicated script,
# same narrow-scope reasoning as every other rule above.
%sudo ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: /usr/libexec/vpinos/vpinos-vr-setup.sh

# vpinos-menu's Main > "Update VPinOS" option (installed systems only)
# -- apt-get update/upgrade need root. Scoped to this one dedicated
# script, which takes no arguments and only runs the same full upgrade
# as `sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade`, same narrow-scope reasoning
# as every other rule above.
%sudo ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: /usr/libexec/vpinos/vpinos-update.sh

# vpinos-menu's Tools > VPX Editor option, when VPX Editor isn't
# installed yet -- apt-get install needs root. Scoped to this one
# dedicated script, which only ever installs the vpx-editor package,
# same narrow-scope reasoning as every other rule above.
%sudo ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: /usr/libexec/vpinos/vpinos-vpx-editor-setup.sh
